{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:ccfb55e0de7db9bf","name":"Old Republic Admiral","source":{"id":"source:reference-ccfb55e0de7db9bf","title":"Old Republic Admiral","revision":19271,"timestamp":"2024-08-25T21:38:14Z","sha256":"c23fec7522c06ff5abdf42d9a95d96bcadcce9a5bc40e684d1ae77f52867a3bd","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=19271","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Old%20Republic%20Admiral&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-ccfb55e0de7db9bf","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Knights of the Old Republic Campaign Guide"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Knights_of_the_Old_Republic_Campaign_Guide"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Affiliations: ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Old Republic"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Old_Republic","referenceId":"reference:6517b7e15507b001"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["From the Admiral of the Fleet to the lowest Rear Admiral, the right to \"raise one's flag\" is the signal achievement for all in the Republic Navy. Of the several kinds of admiral, the full Admirals typify the Naval ideal. Unlike the aged admirals of ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Core Worlds"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Core_Worlds?action=edit&redlink=1"},", they continue to fly for ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Old Republic"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Old_Republic","referenceId":"reference:6517b7e15507b001"},", commanding fleet battles. And while the \"junior flags\"- Vice and Rear Admirals- can still lose their careers after an embarrassing loss, Admirals have enough connections at Admiralty Plaza to survive anything. More important, they have clout at the shipyards, getting priority on repairs and provisions.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Full Admirals do not run their own vessels, instead traveling within the fleet and transferring their command to whatever ship they are on. However, many find ships thy like and captains they enjoy working with- and they have the influence necessary to bring those ships into whatever actions they are mounting.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Each Old Republic Admiral, regardless of rank, receives an office at Admiralty Plaza and the use of a permanent clerical staff. Most Old Republic Admirals eschew the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Coruscant"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Coruscant","referenceId":"reference:2ee37a21e9e7a955"}," work and bring their entourage with them. Secretary to an Admiral is an ideal learning experience for any cadet.\n"]},"\n\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Old Republic Admiral Statistics (CL 15)"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Medium ",{"tag":"a","children":["Human"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Human","referenceId":"reference:9ffa865f2bc6e850"}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Nonheroic"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Nonheroic","referenceId":"reference:1bca2ef1d9ebe1c3"}," 4/",{"tag":"a","children":["Noble"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Noble","referenceId":"reference:190d375ec3483f8f"}," 7/",{"tag":"a","children":["Officer"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Officer","referenceId":"reference:192135a8adabe174"}," 7\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Force Points"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Force_Points"},":"]}," 4\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Initiative"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Initiative","referenceId":"reference:3e687de48a6ad4e5"},":"]}," +19; ",{"tag":"b","children":["Senses:"]}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Perception"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Perception","referenceId":"reference:bd18e320a6bb9f53"}," +21\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Languages:"]}," Basic, Bocce, Bothese, Durese, High Galactic, Mon Calamarian, Sullustese, Zabrak\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Defenses"]},"\n",{"tag":"p